  "helpBrand": "The company that made the phone. Example: Samsung, Vivo, Apple. It is written on the back of the phone. Tap a name below to fill it quickly.",
  "helpModel": "The phone's model name. Example: Galaxy A54, Y21. Find it in Settings > About phone.",
  "helpColour": "The colour of the phone's back. Example: Black, Blue. Helps find the right phone on the shelf.",
  "helpImei": "A 15-digit number that belongs to this one phone only. Dial *#06# on the phone to see it. Copy it from the phone, not from the box — the box can belong to a different phone. Police use this number to trace stolen phones.",
  "helpImei2": "Phones with two SIM slots have a second IMEI. *#06# shows both. Leave empty if there is only one.",
  "helpSerial": "The maker's serial number, found in Settings > About phone. Not needed for most phones — fill it if you have it.",
  "helpPaid": "The money you gave the person who sold you this phone. Example: 6000. Only numbers, no ₹ sign.",
  "helpOtherCost": "Any other money spent on this phone that is not a repair. Example: auto fare to collect it, cleaning, a new cover. Leave empty if none.",
  "helpAsking": "The price you want to sell this phone for. The green box below shows your profit straight away. If it turns red, you will lose money at this price.",
  "helpProfit": "Selling price minus everything spent: what you paid, repairs and other costs. Green means profit, red means loss.",
  "helpRepairs": "Work done to make this phone ready to sell, and what it cost. Example: new battery ₹800. It is added to the cost, so the profit stays correct.",
  "helpBench": "Turn this on if the phone is still being repaired. It will not be shown as ready to sell until you turn it off.",
  "helpGrade": "A letter for how good the phone is. A: everything works. B: 1 to 3 things not working. C: 4 or more not working, or the display was replaced or has white spots. D: damaged, bent or iCloud locked. The app works it out from the checks — tap a letter to choose it yourself.",
  "helpChecklist": "Everything starts as Working. Tap Not working only for what is broken. For questions like \"Display replaced\", tap Yes only if it is true.",
